1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,500
Three robots. Two failed systems. One shared understanding.

2
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:16,322
This is Greg: an AI crew coordinated through a FalkorDB knowledge
graph.

3
00:00:16,322 --> 00:00:24,999
On Orpheus, cooling and communications are degraded. The crew
investigates, until Bolt goes offline.

4
00:00:24,999 --> 00:00:33,313
The engineer transfers to Echo. A different body. A different
location. Shared evidence survives.

5
00:00:33,313 --> 00:00:39,176
Two independent observations connect to one upstream power bus.

6
00:00:39,176 --> 00:00:48,556
The graph determines which tasks are ready, which routes are open,
and which body can act.

7
00:00:48,556 --> 00:00:54,249
Moss delivers the replacement relay. Echo repairs the bus.

8
00:00:54,249 --> 00:00:59,450
The crew verifies both systems before declaring recovery.

9
00:00:59,450 --> 00:01:07,658
These are recorded actions from a real Gemini run, replayed faster
for this film.

10
00:01:07,658 --> 00:01:16,228
Three authored live-model scenarios completed, including a sealed
corridor and a mid-mission body failure.

11
00:01:16,228 --> 00:01:20,151
Sixty deterministic recovery runs also passed.

12
00:01:20,151 --> 00:01:24,000
Greg. Shared knowledge. Distributed action.
